            <ArticleTitle>Ibuprofen and compression bandage in the treatment of ankle sprains.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>322-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One hundred patients with sprained ankles were randomly allocated to treatment with Ibuprofen 800 mg X 3 daily and placebo and to treatment with two qualities of compression bandaging. Neither Ibuprofen nor high quality bandaging had a significant effect on the swelling, pain or tenderness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
